// Project-level base configuration. COMMITTED, and it must be.
//
// WHY THIS FILE IS IN GIT WHEN IT USED TO BE IGNORED. It was gitignored so the
// Apple Team ID would never enter the repository. That protected the value and
// broke the build: Xcode resolves a base-configuration reference when it
// constructs the build description, so a MISSING FILE is a hard error before a
// single source file compiles —
//
//     error: Unable to open base configuration reference file
//            '.../app/ios/Tacendum.xcconfig'
//
// — twice, once per project-level configuration, exit 65. A fresh clone could
// not build the app or the extension AT ALL, which would mean the published
// tree was not Corresponding Source: a stranger cannot rebuild what we ship.
// Found by building from a clean clone.
//
// The repo only ever needed to withhold the VALUE, not the FILE. So this file
// ships with an empty default and pulls the real value from a gitignored
// sibling.
//
// HOW THE DOCUMENTED BEHAVIOUR STAYED WRONG. Tacendum.xcconfig.example claimed
// a missing file left Simulator builds working, citing `xcodebuild
// -showBuildSettings` as proof. That command TOLERATES a missing
// base-configuration reference and simply omits the setting; `xcodebuild build`
// does not. The claim was verified with the one command incapable of detecting
// the failure, and every local build hid it because the ignored file existed on
// this disk.
//
// ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING. xcconfig is last-match-wins, so the empty default MUST
// come first and the include second. Reversed, the empty default clobbers the
// local team ID, `-showBuildSettings` prints nothing for DEVELOPMENT_TEAM,
// Simulator builds still succeed, and device signing breaks invisibly — the
// same class of silent failure this file exists to end.

// Apple Developer Team ID. Empty here, on purpose: a clean clone builds to the
// Simulator and fails a DEVICE build loudly.
TACENDUM_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

// The real value, if this machine has been set up. `#include?` is the optional
// form — absent file, no error.
#include? "Tacendum.local.xcconfig"
